    <section class="oop-section">
        <h2 class="oop-section-title">Concept Overview</h2>
        <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 1.5rem;">
            <li><strong>Code Reuse</strong>: `choose_action` is almost identical to `respond_to_npc`.</li>
            <li><strong>Game Logic</strong>: `compute_damage` implements the rules (`Base - Armour`).</li>
            <li><strong>Math functions</strong>: Using `max(0, ...)` to prevent healing via negative damage.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="oop-section">
        <h2 class="oop-section-title">Common Misconceptions</h2>
        <div class="info-content">
            <p><strong>1. Negative Damage</strong></p>
            <p>If Armour (8) > Damage (5), the result is -3. If we subtract -3 HP, we ADD 3 HP! Students <em>must</em> use `max(0, result)`.</p>
            
            <p><strong>2. Duplicating `print`</strong></p>
            <p>Students often print the list of options inside `choose_action`. The Engine already prints it. If they print it again, it shows twice.</p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="oop-section">
        <h2 class="oop-section-title">Solution Code</h2>
        <div class="code-block" style="background: #1e1e1e; color: #d4d4d4; padding: 1rem; border-radius: 6px; overflow-x: auto;">
            <pre><code>    def choose_action(self, options):
        # Exactly like interaction!
        while True:
            try:
                choice = int(input("Choose action: ")) - 1
                if 0 <= choice < len(options):
                    return choice
                print("Invalid choice.")
            except ValueError:
                print("Please enter a number.")

    def compute_damage(self, base_damage, armour):
        # Prevent negative damage (healing)
        damage = base_damage - armour
        return max(0, damage)

    # Bonus: Critical Hit
    import random
    def calculate_critical_hit(self, base_damage):
        if random.random() < 0.15: # 15% chance
            return (base_damage * 2, True)
        return (base_damage, False)</code></pre>
        </div>
